<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Yamaha Sirius vs Yamaha Mio: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>Comparing rental costs usually means hunting for the cheaper option, but the Yamaha Sirius and Yamaha Mio make that hunt unnecessary. Both models appear on the same verified price list in Hanoi with identical rates for daily, weekly, and monthly rental. That turns this comparison into something more useful: a clear look at what each format delivers for exactly the same money.</p>
<p>This guide compares the two models across price, riding experience, and running costs, so you can decide which one earns your rental days. It builds on the guide to <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a>, fits within the main <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource, and answers practical questions from the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>. Since the Sirius and the Mio are priced identically, the real decision is about which bike fits you.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Two Yamaha options at one price point</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Verified rental prices for both models</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Why the cost is identical</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">Riding the Yamaha Sirius in Hanoi</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">Riding the Yamaha Mio in Hanoi</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">Fuel economy and daily running costs</a></li>
